\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {A}: Perceived Difficulty versus Objective Difficulty. Numbers refer to the question ID (see Materials). The red dashed line represents the optimal estimation. \textbf  {B}: Estimated Conditional Probability versus True Conditional Probability. Each data point is a pair of two questions. The red line represents the optimal prediction while the dark line represents the fit of the linear model. \textbf  {C}: Conditional robabilities estmiated by the Main Model vs True Conditional Probability. Each data point is a pair of two questions. The red line represents the optimal prediction while the dark line represents the fit of the linear model.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
